  </script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/EstimateForm.fIc_XS_5.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/IdeaPage.BMJ8XAQx.css"></head> <body class> <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>  <main id="main"> <header class="hd" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <div class="wrap hd__in" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a class="hd__logo" href="/" aria-label="Maverick City Builders home" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <span class="hd__mark" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>MCB</span> <span class="hd__name" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Maverick City Builders</span> </a> <nav class="hd__nav" aria-label="Primary" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <details class="hd__drop" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <summary data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Services</summary> <ul data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Kitchen remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Bathroom remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>General renovations</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Carpentry</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Deck building</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Interior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Exterior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Building restoration</a></li><li data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Water damage restoration</a></li></ul> </details> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Painting</a> <a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Our work</a> <a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Areas we serve</a> <a href="/about" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>About</a> </nav> <div class="hd__act" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a class="hd__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> <a class="btn hd__cta" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <button class="hd__burger" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mnav" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span><span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span> </button> </div> </div> <nav class="mnav" id="mnav" hidden aria-label="Mobile" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Kitchen remodeling</a><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Bathroom remodeling</a><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>General renovations</a><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Carpentry</a><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Deck building</a><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Interior painting</a><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Exterior painting</a><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Building restoration</a><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Water damage restoration</a> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Painting</a><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Our work</a><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Areas we serve</a> <a href="/about" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>About</a><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <a class="mnav__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> </div> </nav> </header> <script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.hd__burger`),t=document.getElementById(`mnav`);e?.addEventListener(`click`,()=>{let n=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,String(!n)),t&&(t.hidden=n),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,n?`Open menu`:`Close menu`)});</script> <main id="main" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <section class="top wrap-wide" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <div data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>/</span> <a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Carpentry</a></nav> <h1 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Interior Doors and Closets</h1> <p class="cost" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Typical Central MA range: <strong data-astro-cid-j5amansv>$300–$1,100 per interior door installed (typical Central MA range)</strong></p> <p class="lead" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Solid-core doors that close quietly, old openings that finally latch, and closets that hold what you own.</p> <a class="btn" href="#estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Book a free in-home consultation</a> </div> <figure data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <img src="/ideas/interior-doors-and-closets-main.webp" alt="Design idea: upstairs hallway in a New England colonial with painted two-panel solid-core doors and matching casing" width="1600" height="1195" fetchpriority="high" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <figcaption data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Design idea (AI illustration) — not an MCB project photo.</figcaption> </figure> </section> <article class="wrap prose" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 id="who-this-work-is-right-for-and-when-a-door-isnt-the-problem">Who this work is right for, and when a door isn’t the problem</h2>
<p>New interior doors change how a house feels every day: quieter bedrooms, doors that latch on the first push, and a consistent style from room to room. Closet work gets the most out of the smallest rooms in the house. Both are good projects when:</p>
<ul>
<li>Doors are hollow, dented, mismatched or don’t latch.</li>
<li>You are painting or re-trimming anyway, so new casing goes on at the same time.</li>
<li>Closets are a single rod and a shelf, and half the space is wasted.</li>
</ul>
<p>When a door isn’t the problem:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Doors that suddenly start rubbing across a whole floor</strong> usually point to settling, a sagging beam or a moisture problem. A new door won’t fix a racked opening for long.</li>
<li><strong>A closet on a cold exterior wall with musty smells</strong> needs air and possibly insulation work before shelving.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/carpentry">carpentry</a> page covers the full list of finish work. This page gets into door types, fitting doors in older homes and building out closets.</p>
<h2 id="pre-hung-vs-slab-solid-vs-hollow">Pre-hung vs slab, solid vs hollow</h2>
<p><strong>Pre-hung doors</strong> come hung on hinges in a new jamb. The old jamb and casing come out, the new unit is set plumb and shimmed, and new casing goes on. It is the cleaner result when openings are out of square or casing is being replaced anyway.</p>
<p><strong>Slab doors</strong> are just the door. They get hinge mortises and a bore for the latch cut to match the existing jamb. That’s the right move when the original jamb and casing are worth keeping, which is often the case in 1920s–40s homes with good painted trim. Fitting a slab to an old opening takes time: the opening is rarely square, so the door is planed to follow it.</p>
<p><strong>Hollow-core</strong> doors have a cardboard-honeycomb core. Light, cheap and fine for closets.</p>
<p><strong>Solid-core</strong> doors have a composite wood core. Heavier, quieter, and a better feel for bedrooms, baths and offices.</p>
<p><strong>Solid wood</strong> doors are stile-and-rail construction. They look the part in older homes but move more with the seasons.</p>
<h2 id="what-doors-and-closets-cost-in-central-ma">What doors and closets cost in Central MA</h2>
<p>Typical Central Massachusetts ranges, not quotes. Your written estimate itemises each opening, the door and hardware, casing, painting and exclusions.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Typical scope</th>
<th>Typical range</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Hollow-core pre-hung door, new casing one side</td>
<td>$300–$550 per door</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Solid-core pre-hung door, new casing both sides</td>
<td>$550–$1,100 per door</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Slab door fitted to an existing jamb</td>
<td>$250–$600 per door</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Bifold or bypass closet doors</td>
<td>$300–$900 per opening</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Pocket door in an existing wall, including wall patch</td>
<td>$1,500–$3,500</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Reach-in closet shelving and rods, custom</td>
<td>$800–$3,500</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Walk-in closet system</td>
<td>$2,500–$9,000</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>New closet framed into a room, with door</td>
<td>$2,500–$6,000</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Paint, hardware grade and whether casing is replaced move these numbers more than the door itself.</p>
<h2 id="what-the-job-involves-step-by-step">What the job involves, step by step</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Measure every opening.</strong> Older homes are full of non-standard sizes: 6’6” tall doors, 2’4” and 2’6” widths, and jambs of odd depths over thick plaster. Each opening is measured, not assumed.</li>
<li><strong>Order doors and hardware.</strong> Pre-hung units are ordered to jamb depth and swing; slabs are ordered to size and fitted on site.</li>
<li><strong>Remove old doors and trim.</strong> In pre-1978 homes, doors, jambs and casing often carry old lead paint. Removing or planing them is paint-disturbing work under EPA lead-safe rules; ask any contractor for their lead-safe certification in writing before that work starts.</li>
<li><strong>Set and fit.</strong> Pre-hung units are shimmed plumb and square with even gaps. Slabs are scribed, planed and hung. Doors are undercut where a hot-air return needs air to pass.</li>
<li><strong>Hardware and casing.</strong> Latches, strikes and stops adjusted so the door closes with light pressure. New casing mitered, glued and nailed.</li>
<li><strong>Closets.</strong> Shelving hung on cleats or a rail system into framing, rods at heights that fit what you store.</li>
<li><strong>Finish.</strong> Fill, caulk and paint. All six sides of a new door get sealed.</li>
</ol>
<p>Timeline: a typical scope looks like one to two days for a handful of doors, three to five days for a whole floor, plus paint. Closet systems are usually one to two days each.</p>
<h2 id="new-england-specifics-seasons-settling-and-old-openings">New England specifics: seasons, settling and old openings</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Seasonal swelling.</strong> In July a wood door can gain enough width to rub. Fitting doors with consistent gaps and sealing the top and bottom edges, which are often skipped, keeps that in check.</li>
<li><strong>Settled openings.</strong> In older colonials in Lancaster and Sterling, and in mill-era homes in Clinton, the header over a door may have dropped a little over a century. We shim and plane to suit, and flag it when the framing needs attention first.</li>
<li><strong>Thick walls.</strong> Plaster and lath make walls deeper than standard jambs. Jamb extensions or custom jambs make up the difference.</li>
<li><strong>Cold closets.</strong> Closets on exterior walls in older homes can run cold and damp. Ventilated shelving and a louvered or undercut door help air move.</li>
<li><strong>Capes and knee walls.</strong> In 1940s–60s capes common in Worcester and Leominster, the upstairs has knee-wall storage behind short doors. A built-in drawer bank or a proper insulated access door is often a better use of that space than a crawl-in hatch.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="how-to-choose-doors-and-closet-options">How to choose doors and closet options</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Style:</strong> Shaker two-panel or five-panel doors suit most colonials and newer homes; six-panel for traditional; flat slab for modern. Match what the rest of the house has.</li>
<li><strong>Core:</strong> solid-core for rooms where people sleep, work or bathe; hollow-core for closets.</li>
<li><strong>Hardware finish:</strong> one finish across the floor looks deliberate. Lever handles are easier for kids and older hands.</li>
<li><strong>Closet layout:</strong> double-hang rods for shirts and pants, one long-hang section, adjustable shelves for folded clothes, drawers only where you really need them since they add cost fast.</li>
<li><strong>Closet material:</strong> wire is cheapest, melamine and laminate systems are the middle, painted wood is the premium option.</li>
</ul>
<p>Pairing new doors with new trim? See <a href="/carpentry/trim-crown-and-wainscoting">trim, crown and wainscoting</a>. If you want storage beyond a closet, look at <a href="/carpentry/built-ins-and-mudrooms">built-ins and mudrooms</a>.</p>
<h2 id="what-to-ask-any-contractor-about-doors-and-closets">What to ask any contractor about doors and closets</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pre-hung or slab for each opening, and why?</li>
<li>Solid-core or hollow-core, and which rooms get which?</li>
<li>Are all six sides of the doors sealed or painted?</li>
<li>Is casing replaced on both sides, and is painting included?</li>
<li>In a pre-1978 home, who removes the old doors and trim, and can I see their lead-safe certification in writing?</li>
<li>What exactly is in the written estimate, and what is excluded?</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="start-with-a-measure">Start with a measure</h2>
<p>We can come out, measure each opening and closet, show door and hardware options and give you a written estimate. The consultation is free.</p>
 <section class="faq" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Common questions</h2> <details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Should I buy pre-hung doors or just new slabs?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Pre-hung is usually faster and more reliable when the old jambs are worn, out of square or you are changing casing anyway. A slab makes sense when the existing jambs and trim are worth keeping, which is common in older homes with original casing you don&#39;t want to disturb.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Is a solid-core door worth the extra cost?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>For bedrooms, bathrooms and home offices, usually yes. Solid-core doors block noise better, feel heavier and close with a firm sound. For closets and linen cabinets, hollow-core is fine and saves money.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Why do my doors stick in summer and gap in winter?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Wood doors and jambs take on moisture in humid months and release it in dry, heated months. A door fitted too tight in January binds in July. Sealing all six sides of a door and fitting it with the right gaps helps a lot. Sticking can also be the house settling, which is a framing issue, not a door issue.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Can you put in a pocket door in an existing wall?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Often, but the wall has to be opened, it cannot hold plumbing, ductwork or much wiring in the pocket side, and if it is a bearing wall the header needs to be sized for the wider opening. We check before we price it.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>What door goes between the garage and the house?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>The code calls for a fire-resistant door there, such as solid wood or solid or honeycomb-core steel at least 1-3/8 inches thick, or a 20-minute fire-rated door. Some towns also look for a self-closing device. Your building department confirms what applies.</p></details> </section> </article> <section class="wrap-wide more" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>More carpentry ideas</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/carpentry/built-ins-and-mudrooms" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/built-ins-and-mudrooms-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a painted built-in cabinet scribed tight to an uneven plaster wall" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Built-Ins and Mudroom Storage</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/carpentry/trim-crown-and-wainscoting" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/trim-crown-and-wainscoting-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a coped inside corner of painted crown molding" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Crown Molding, Trim and Wainscoting</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/carpentry/stairs-and-railings" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/stairs-and-railings-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a stained oak stair tread with a rounded nosing over a white painted riser" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Interior Stairs and Railings</span></a></li> </ul> <p data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Back to carpentry</a></p> </section> <div id="estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><form class="ef" id="estimate-form" novalidate data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-name" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Name <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-name" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please tell us your name.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-phone" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-phone" name="phone" type="tel" inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-phone" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We need a phone number to reach you.</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</label> <input id="ef-email" name="email" type="email" inputmode="email" autocomplete="email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-email" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>That email address doesn't look right.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-town" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project town <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-town" name="town" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-town" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Which town is the project in?</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-type" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project type <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <select id="ef-type" name="projectType" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Choose one…</option> <option value="Kitchen remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Kitchen remodeling</option><option value="Bathroom remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Bathroom remodeling</option><option value="General renovations" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>General renovations</option><option value="Carpentry" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Carpentry</option><option value="Deck building" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Deck building</option><option value="Interior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Interior painting</option><option value="Exterior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Exterior painting</option><option value="Building restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Building restoration</option><option value="Water damage restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Water damage restoration</option> <option value="Multiple / not sure" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Multiple, or not sure yet</option> </select> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-type" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please pick the closest match.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-details" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project details <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <textarea id="ef-details" name="projectDetails" rows="5" required placeholder="What you want done, roughly when, and anything you already know about the space." data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></textarea> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-details" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>A sentence or two is plenty.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Desired timing</label> <select id="ef-timing" name="timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>No strong preference</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>As soon as possible</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 1–3 months</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 3–6 months</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Later this year</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Just planning / budgeting</option> </select> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-contact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Preferred contact</label> <select id="ef-contact" name="preferredContact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone call</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Text message</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</option> </select> </div> </div> <!-- Honeypot. Off-screen, aria-hidden, never focusable. --> <div class="ef__hp" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-company" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Company</label> <input id="ef-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> </div> <p class="ef__consent" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>
By sending this you agree we can contact you about your project by phone, text or email.
    Message rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out of texts at any time. We don't sell your details.
</p> <button class="btn ef__submit" type="submit" data-ev="form_submit" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Send it over</button> <p class="ef__note" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We read every one of these. Prefer to talk?
<a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> <p class="ef__fail" id="ef-fail" role="alert" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></p> </form> <div class="ef__ok" id="ef-ok" role="status" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <h3 data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Got it.</h3> <p data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Your details are with us. We'll be in touch to arrange a look at the project.
     If it's urgent, call <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> </div> <script>(function(){const CRM = {"endpoint":"https://backend.leadconnectorhq.com/external-tracking/events","locationId":"b5lmCvdlpVkhC4JOVBjd","trackingId":"tk_e76468050a3e42e0b65b2fa5b3c87a7f"};
const PHONE = "(508) 656-7436";
const EMAIL = "douglas@mcitybuilders.com";

  const form = document.getElementById('estimate-form');
  const okBox = document.getElementById('ef-ok');
  const failBox = document.getElementById('ef-fail');
  if (form) {
    const started = Date.now();
    let announcedStart = false;
    form.addEventListener('input', () => {
      if (!announcedStart && typeof gtag === 'function') {
        announcedStart = true;
        gtag('event', 'form_start', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate' });   // no field contents
      }
    }, { once: false });

    const showErr = (el, on) => {
      el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', String(on));
      const p = form.querySelector('[data-err="' + el.id + '"]');
      if (p) p.hidden = !on;
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      failBox.hidden = true;

      // --- validation with real messages, focus moved to the first problem
      let firstBad = null;
      for (const el of form.querySelectorAll('[required]')) {
        const bad = !el.value.trim();
        showErr(el, bad);
        if (bad && !firstBad) firstBad = el;
      }
      const em = form.querySelector('#ef-email');
      const emBad = em.value.trim() !== '' && !/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]{2,}$/.test(em.value.trim());
      showErr(em, emBad);
      if (emBad && !firstBad) firstBad = em;
      if (firstBad) { firstBad.focus(); return; }

      // --- bot gates: hidden field filled, or submitted faster than a human types
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      if (String(fd.get('company') || '').trim() !== '' || Date.now() - started < 3000) {
        form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false; return;   // silent, nothing sent
      }

      const btn = form.querySelector('.ef__submit');
      const label = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Sending…'; btn.disabled = true;

      let ss = null; try { ss = sessionStorage; } catch (_) {}
      const attr = (k) => { try { return (ss && ss.getItem('mcb_' + k)) || ''; } catch (_) { return ''; } };

      const payload = {
        type: 'external_form_submission',
        timestamp: Date.now(),
        formId: 'Estimate Request',
        formData: {
          full_name: fd.get('name'),
          phone: fd.get('phone'),
          email: fd.get('email') || '',          // logical OR. Not a pipe.
          'contact.project_details': fd.get('projectDetails'),
          project_town: fd.get('town'),
          project_type: fd.get('projectType'),
          timing: fd.get('timing') || '',
          preferred_contact: fd.get('preferredContact') || '',
          utm_source: attr('utm_source'), utm_medium: attr('utm_medium'),
          utm_campaign: attr('utm_campaign'), utm_term: attr('utm_term'),
          utm_content: attr('utm_content'), gclid: attr('gclid'), fbclid: attr('fbclid'),
          landing_page: attr('mcb_landing') || attr('landing'),
          referrer: attr('referrer') || document.referrer || '',
          Timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
        },
        url: location.href, title: document.title, path: location.pathname,
        userAgent: navigator.userAgent,
        trackingId: CRM.trackingId, locationId: CRM.locationId,
        sessionId: (crypto && crypto.randomUUID) ? crypto.randomUUID() : String(Math.random()).slice(2),
      };

      let ok = false, diag = '';
      try {
        const res = await fetch(CRM.endpoint, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', version: '2021-07-28' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        ok = res.ok; diag = 'HTTP ' + res.status;
      } catch (err) { diag = 'network: ' + (err && err.message); }

      if (!ok) {
        // Nothing reached the CRM. Keep every keystroke on screen, give a real
        // route through, and do NOT report a conversion.
        console.error('[MCB estimate form]', diag);
        btn.textContent = label; btn.disabled = false;
        failBox.innerHTML = 'We couldn\'t send that from the website. Please call ' +
          '<a href="tel:+15086567436">' + PHONE + '</a> or email ' +
          '<a href="mailto:' + EMAIL + '">' + EMAIL + '</a>. ' +
          'Everything you typed is still in the form above.';
        failBox.hidden = false;
        failBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        return;
      }

      if (typeof gtag === 'function') {
        gtag('event', 'generate_lead', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate', lead_source: 'website_estimate_form' });
      }
      form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false;
      okBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      okBox.querySelector('h3').setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
      okBox.querySelector('h3').focus();
    });
  }
})();</script></div> </main> <footer class="ft" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__top" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Maverick City Builders</span> <p class="ft__pitch" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General contracting and remodeling across Massachusetts.</p> <a class="btn btn--onDark" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Request an estimate</a> </div> <nav aria-label="Services" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Services</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Kitchen remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Bathroom remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General renovations</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Carpentry</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Deck building</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Interior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Exterior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Building restoration</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Water damage restoration</a></li></ul> </nav> <nav aria-label="Company" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Company</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/about" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>About</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Our work</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Areas we serve</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/blog" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Articles</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</a></li> </ul> </nav> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</h2> <address class="ft__nap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>(508) 656-7436</a> <a href="mailto:douglas@mcitybuilders.com" data-ev="email_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>douglas@mcitybuilders.com</a> <span data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>1171 Main St<br data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Lancaster, MA 01523</span> <em data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Office visits by appointment</em> </address> </div> </div> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__base" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>&copy; 2026 Maverick City Builders &middot; Lancaster, Massachusetts</p> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/privacy-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="/terms" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Terms</a> &middot;
<a href="/accessibility" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Accessibility</a> &middot; <a href="/cookie-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Cookies</a></p> </div> </div> </footer> </main>  <div id="mcb-cookie-banner" hidden role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Cookie choices" style="position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:99999;background:#0b0b0b;border-top:2px solid #E10600;color:#e6e6e6;padding:18px 20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center"> <span style="max-width:640px">We measure page views with Google Analytics in cookieless mode. Accept to allow analytics cookies and ad measurement; Decline to stay cookieless. Read our <a href="/cookie-policy" style="color:#ff6b6b;text-decoration:underline">Cookie Policy</a>.</span> <span style="display:flex;gap:10px"> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-decline" style="background:transparent;color:#e6e6e6;border:1px solid #777;padding:12px 20px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Decline</button> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-accept" style="background:#E10600;color:#fff;border:0;padding:12px 22px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Accept</button> </span> </div> <!-- Analytics with Google Consent Mode (mcb-consent-v2, 2026-09-18, Doug's decision).
       GA4 loads by default with analytics_storage DENIED = cookieless pings, no _ga cookie.
       Accept upgrades consent to granted. Browsers sending Do-Not-Track or Global Privacy
       Control get nothing at all. The static site does the same via patch_consent.py. --> <script>(function(){const ga4 = "G-7HXJQJL5Q2";

    (function () {
      var KEY = 'mcb-consent'; // MUST match the static site's key (hyphen). An underscore here meant GA4 never loaded on any Astro page.
      var dnt = false;
      try { dnt = navigator.doNotTrack == '1' || window.doNotTrack == '1' || !!navigator.globalPrivacyControl; } catch (e) {}
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      window.gtag = function () { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); };
      gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied',
        analytics_storage: 'denied', functionality_storage: 'granted', security_storage: 'granted' });
      function load() {
        if (window.__mcbTagged) return; window.__mcbTagged = true;
        var s = document.createElement('script'); s.async = true;
        s.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + ga4;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
        gtag('js', new Date()); gtag('config', ga4);
      }
      function boot() { // Accept: cookies + ad measurement allowed
        gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ad_user_data: 'granted', ad_personalization: 'granted', analytics_storage: 'granted' });
        load();
      }
      var stored = null;
      try { stored = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (e) {}
      if (stored === 'granted') boot();
      else if (!dnt) load(); // undecided or declined: cookieless measurement only
      window.__mcbConsentBoot = boot;
      // Same banner as the static site. Without it a visitor who LANDS on a town page
      // is never asked, so is never measured.
      try {
        var v = localStorage.getItem(KEY), b = document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-banner');
        if (b && v !== 'granted' && v !== 'denied') {
          b.hidden = false;
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-accept').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'granted'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; boot(); });
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-decline').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'denied'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; });
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      // lightweight, non-sensitive interaction events
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var a = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-ev]');
        if (a && typeof window.gtag === 'function') {
          gtag('event', a.getAttribute('data-ev'), { link_url: a.getAttribute('href') || '' });
        }
      }, true);
    })();
  })();</script></body> </html>